## Third-Party Context Providers

Any library component that uses React hooks internally (`useContext`, `useState`, etc.) crashes when rendered in a Server Component. The React dispatcher is null during server rendering.

**Audit rule**: Before importing any third-party component, check if it uses hooks. If unsure, assume it does and wrap in a Client Component.

```tsx
// BAD — SessionProvider uses useContext internally, crashes in Server Component
import { SessionProvider } from 'next-auth/react';

export default function RootLayout({ children }) {
  return <SessionProvider session={session}>{children}</SessionProvider>;
}

// GOOD — import a Client Component wrapper
import { Providers } from '@/components/providers'; // has "use client"

export default function RootLayout({ children }) {
  return <Providers session={session}>{children}</Providers>;
}
```

**Common context providers that crash in Server Components**: `SessionProvider` (next-auth), Radix UI primitives (TooltipProvider, Dialog, etc.), theme providers, any `createContext` consumer.

