## Type Safety

### No `Record<string, unknown>` for Known Shapes

When the shape is known, define an interface:

```tsx
// BAD — loses type safety
const audience: Record<string, unknown> = {
  interests: ["tech", "design"],
};
const interests = audience.interests; // Error: unknown

// GOOD — typed
interface Audience {
  interests: string[];
}
const audience: Audience = {
  interests: ["tech", "design"],
};
```

### No `as any` Casting

```tsx
// BAD
const user = session.user as any;

// GOOD
const user = session.user as { name: string; workspaceId: string };

// BETTER — define a type
interface SessionUser {
  name: string;
  workspaceId: string;
}
const user = session.user as SessionUser;
```

### Exhaustive Switch/Map Guards

Always provide a fallback when mapping from string keys:

```tsx
// GOOD — has fallback
const cfg = statusConfig[status] ?? statusConfig.DRAFT;
const IconComponent = statusIcons[name] ?? DefaultIcon;
```

